 "description": "The doubled picture of Picturing Quantum Processes: thick wires are quantum, thin wires classical. White dots with thin and thick legs measure (thick in, thin out), encode (thin in, thick out), copy and delete; ⏚ discards. The proofs: measuring then deleting is discarding, encoding then discarding is deleting, measuring then encoding is decoherence, discarding a pure state gives the Born rule, and a doubled unitary is causal.",
